The page calls October a separate incident from the March TeamPCP attack, and its stealer the same class of startup trick. The four topics are the page's related defense topics.
notes:
The page links one other kill chain, and four defense topics.

It calls this a separate incident from the March TeamPCP attack, which has its own kill chain, and says the October stealer used the same class of Python startup trick as the March attack. After March, LiteLLM hardened its releases; the October attack went around those controls.

The page's related defense topics are CI/CD security, GitHub Actions security, AI/ML security and AWS security. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery, and AI/ML for artificial intelligence and machine learning.
